  <div class="spine page-head">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="lede">Please read before using this tool.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose-spine prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Portfolio Lab is for <strong>educational and informational purposes only</strong>.
      It does not constitute investment advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Not SEBI-registered</h2>
    <p>
      Portfolio Lab and its author are <strong>not registered with SEBI</strong> as an
      investment adviser, portfolio manager, research analyst, or any other regulated category.
      Nothing on this site should be construed as regulated financial advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Forward returns are estimates</h2>
    <p>
      All expected-return figures are forward-looking estimates based on publicly available
      research and analyst forecasts. They are <strong>not guarantees</strong>. Actual returns
      may be significantly higher or lower — including total loss of principal.
    </p>
    <p>
      Equity markets can fall <strong>40–60%</strong> peak-to-trough over a full cycle. The
      bear-scenario projection bands in the studio reflect this, but do not capture all tail
      risks.
    </p>

    <h2>Past performance</h2>
    <p>
      Historical CAGR figures shown are for reference only. Past performance is
      <strong>not indicative of future results</strong>. Several trailing-return figures in
      the dataset are artificially elevated by the 2020–2025 bull market and the one-off 2025
      gold rally.
    </p>

    <h2>P2P lending specific risk</h2>
    <p>
      P2P lending is shown for completeness. Advertised returns of 10–18% are gross/pre-default
      marketing figures. RBI (Aug-2024) banned assured-return marketing and credit guarantees.
      Lenders bear 100% of default loss. There is no deposit insurance. This is a high-risk,
      illiquid, slab-taxed instrument.
    </p>

    <h2>Do your own research</h2>
    <p>
      Before making any investment, consult a SEBI-registered investment adviser. Consider
      your own financial situation, tax position, risk tolerance, and investment horizon.
    </p>

    <h2>No liability</h2>
    <p>
      The author accepts no liability for any investment decisions made based on information
      presented on this site. Use at your own risk.
    </p>
  </div>
